{"type":"text","timestamp":1794527403258,"sessionID":"ses_e2dd8cacaffeYX7eAhuv52v3jL","part":{"id":"prt_1d22b0f1c002RtffLlW2Ty2FGk","sessionID":"ses_e2dd8cacaffeYX7eAhuv52v3jL","messageID":"msg_1d22ab8f70013TGJqhB9QYo03f","type":"text","text":"T017 implemented. Here is what changed and the verification evidence.\n\n**File written:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`\n\n- Imported `commandRowFor` from `./command-attach.js`.\n- Added `commandLabel(recommendation)`: builds `<ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)` from the recommendation's own `command`/`policy`/`ownerSkillId`, falling back per field to `commandRowFor(skill)`, dropping `(<policy>)` when no policy is known, and sanitizing every rendered part with `sanitizeSkillLabel`.\n- Used that label for the `use` head (`topLabel`) and for both sides of the `ambiguous` head (`topLabel` and `vsLabel`).\n- Rewrote `doctorCommandString` to read `commandRowFor(id)?.command` for a doctor id and sanitize it.\n- Left the `Also:` companion trigger and its rendering unchanged.\n- No checkbox in `tasks.md` was ticked, and no other file or git state was touched.\n\n**Verify (`$TC`, then the `rg` check):**\n\n```\n$ npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run typecheck\n> typecheck\n> ../../system-spec-kit/node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit --composite false -p tsconfig.build.json\nTC_EXIT=0\n\n$ rg -n \"DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS\\[\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts\nRG_EXIT=1\n```\n\n`tsc` exits 0 with no output, and the `rg` pattern matches nothing (exit 1 is the expected no-match result).\n\n**Not done:** nothing else was requested. The remaining `GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS` block stays in place because T020 owns its deletion; it is now unused until then.","time":{"start":1794527399708,"end":1794527403258}}}
